Aerie-Purpose: Create the per-profile Tab Model service when a profile is created, so it is bound to the tab strips from the first window.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/profiles (chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #176. TabModelServiceFactory (chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model, in the overlay) is a
ProfileKeyedServiceFactory that is created with the browser context, like
PinnedTabServiceFactory beside it. Building the service does no disk work: it posts the read
of AerieTabModel/state.json to the thread pool. The line sits in the desktop-only block.

--- a/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/profiles/BUILD.gn
@@ -733,4 +733,5 @@
     "//chrome/browser/accessibility",
     "//chrome/browser/account_settings",
+    "//chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model",
     "//chrome/browser/affiliations",
     "//chrome/browser/ai",
--- a/chrome/browser/profiles/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/profiles/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc
@@ -16,4 +16,5 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/account_settings/account_setting_service_factory.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/actor/actor_keyed_service_factory.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model/tab_model_service_factory.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/affiliations/affiliation_service_factory.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ai/ai_data_keyed_service_factory.h"
@@ -1293,4 +1294,5 @@
   PersonalContextServiceFactory::GetInstance();
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+  aerie_tab_model::TabModelServiceFactory::GetInstance();
   PinnedTabServiceFactory::GetInstance();
   PinnedToolbarActionsModelFactory::GetInstance();
